 for this gene; some variants represent read-through transcripts that include exons from the upstream gene C17orf86. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2011].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q92503","text":"May play a role in innate immunity by inhibiting the antiviral RIG-I signaling pathway. In this pathway, functions as a negative regulator of RIGI, the cytoplasmic sensor of viral nucleic acids. Prevents the interaction of RIGI with MAVS/IPS1, an important step in signal propagation (PubMed:23843640). May also regulate the SLC18A3 and SLC5A7 cholinergic transporters (PubMed:17092608)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}